[36m(main_task pid=3452925)[0m Doc 1(Title: "Judiciary of Texas") In recent years, municipal courts and justice court in Texas have become the primary venue for acts of misconduct committed by children. Within the city limits, these courts have shared jurisdiction with the JP courts on Class C criminal misdemeanor cases, and have exclusive jurisdiction on cases involving city ordinances. Municipal courts have limited civil jurisdiction over public matters relating to public safety (e.g., dangerous dog determinations). Confusion surrounding a municipal court's civil jurisdiction is complicated that if a municipal court is a ""court of record,"" the Legislature has authorized municipalities to adopt ordinances that give municipal courts concurrent jurisdiction
